From d1bcd9e57dd3aa219e5efb62579e9b002538ba2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:53:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] antinomie: capture the launched program's executable image

Keep a copy of the file a launch executed, for static analysis on the
host, taken from the file the kernel actually opened for the exec rather
than from the path, which the program may rewrite or delete at once.

EXEC with the SPECIMEN flag appends a size limit (1 byte to 64 MiB) and
a time limit (1 to 5000 ms); the copy is read from the opened image at
the exec and the EXEC reply carries its id, size and status. ACQUIRE
copies a file by path the same way. SPECIMEN_READ returns the copy in
pieces, and SPECIMEN_RELEASE drops it. One copy runs at a time, at most
four are kept, their memory is reserved from a 64 MiB budget until it
is really freed, and an unread copy expires after 180 s. A failed copy
never changes the launch's result. A script's copy is the script: what
its interpreter reads later is not covered.

Hooked kernel file:
- fs/exec.c hands the opened image to the capture at the exec of a
  launched program, the one point where the kernel holds the file that
  is about to run.

Contract: revision 10 (EXEC_SPECIMEN, ACQUIRE, SPECIMEN_READ,
SPECIMEN_RELEASE). EXEC with flags becomes possible from this patch:
the EXEC header flags word was zero before.
---
 fs/exec.c                         |   1 +
 include/linux/antinomie_monitor.h |   3 +
 kernel/antinomie/Makefile         |   1 +
 kernel/antinomie/control.c        |  45 ++-
 kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h   |  22 +-
 kernel/antinomie/specimen.c       | 491 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel/antinomie/specimen.h       |  17 ++
 7 files changed, 575 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 kernel/antinomie/specimen.c
 create mode 100644 kernel/antinomie/specimen.h

diff --git a/fs/exec.c b/fs/exec.c
index 718cdfa..81ca5e9 100644
--- a/fs/exec.c
+++ b/fs/exec.c
@@ -1880,6 +1880,7 @@ static int bprm_execve(struct linux_binprm *bprm)
 	if (retval)
 		goto out;
 
+	ant_monitor_specimen_exec(bprm->file);
 	retval = exec_binprm(bprm);
 	if (retval < 0)
 		goto out;
